        "locator": "OSM way 101986702 (French section) + way 317397424 (Italian section), joined at the border (35 m gap between their nearest endpoints), as of 2026-09-18T22:47:00Z",
        "note": "Kept 'approximate' rather than pushed to 'verified' even though the length check passes at 0.06%: as of 28 July 2025 the Fréjus road tunnel has TWO parallel tubes (the original 1980 bore and a new one built 2019-2025, each ~12.9 km, one-way in opposite directions per src:geo-modane-sftrf-second-tube-pr), and the two OSM ways used here carry inconsistent tags (the Italian way is tagged opening_date=2023-10, suggesting it may already describe the new tube rather than the 1980 original that the laboratory was actually excavated beside). Since both tubes run closely parallel over their whole length and this session could not fetch Overpass to disambiguate cleanly, the traced line is treated as approximate for either tube. See the facility worklog.",
